# Verified byte-identical (SHA-256 fingerprint of the DER encoding) to the
# certificate installed by Zscaler on a real GDS-managed macOS device. This
# is Zscaler's generic vendor-default root CA, not an organisation-specific
# certificate, so relying on it here is safe for any Zscaler-managed device.
#
# Pinned fingerprint (see tests/test_ca.py and
# .github/workflows/cert-drift.yml, which checks weekly for upstream drift):
#   sha256: 04:f6:1f:1d:13:aa:e1:d1:65:73:dc:2c:37:f7:96:fd:
#           f4:ac:97:71:3a:69:59:eb:b1:1d:24:73:95:8b:1a:53
#
# Do not hand-edit this file. To update, replace it with alphagov's current
# copy, re-run tests/test_ca.py to get the new fingerprint, and update the
# EXPECTED_SHA256_FINGERPRINT constant there.
